## Step 1, the plan and the worst case

- Task 4 of plan.md becomes `[~]`, then `[b] ... deferred:maker` again in the evidence commit.
- The worst case of D11 goes into spend-log.tsv before the calls: 3 calls, the item (a) spend of
  0.06 USD, the guard stop of 0.15 USD, and the stop per call above 0.03 USD. The highest call cost
  seen in item (a) is 0.01 USD, so the worst case is 0.03 USD for the 3 calls. The sum of 0.06 USD
  and 0.03 USD is 0.09 USD, under the 0.15 USD stop, so the pool ran.

## Step 2, the network check and the 3 calls

- The network check of the PM order runs before each paid call:
  `curl -sS -m 20 -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models`. It sends no
  key and it costs nothing. A call runs only when the check gives 200. A failed check waits 60 s and
  checks again, up to 5 times. A failed check uses no try.
- The first check failed with a DNS timeout and gave the code 000. The retry after 60 s gave 200.
  The 3 checks before the 3 calls gave 200, 200, and 200.
- The 3 calls ran one after another. The guard refused no call. Each call cost 0.01 USD, and no
  call was above 0.03 USD.

